SUMMARY:Application deadline: ERC Starting Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ERC. For researchers post-PhD (eligibility widened to 10 years
  from 2027). Up to €1.5M for 5 years. Bottom-up: any research topic. Ca
 ll opens July 2026\, deadline 14 October 2026.\n\nhttps://erc.europa.eu/a
 pply-grant/starting-grant
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/starting-grant
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-199-20261016@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Application deadline: EWUU i4PH Seed Call 2026 – Preventive heal
 th transitions
DESCRIPTION:EWUU Alliance – Institute 4 Preventive Health (i4PH). Seed f
 unding from the TU/e–WUR–UU–UMCU alliance for transdisciplinary pre
 ventive-health projects that fit an i4PH research line (healthy start\, h
 ealthy living environments\, future of cancer\, health at home) and a tra
 nsition pathway (incl. 'planetary-centred'). Meant to produce a tangible 
 next step such as a Horizon Europe or NWA application\, white paper or re
 view. Total €200k\, about 4–5 projects\; projects start from 1 Jan 20
 27 and budget must be spent before 1 Dec 2027.\n\nhttps://preventivehealt
 h.ewuu.nl/2026/06/seed-call-for-preventive-health-transitions-building-th
 e-future-of-preventive-health/
URL:https://preventivehealth.ewuu.nl/2026/06/seed-call-for-preventive-heal
 th-transitions-building-the-future-of-preventive-health/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-204-20261020@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Call for Validation of Biomarker Candidates
  2027
DESCRIPTION:KWF (Dutch Cancer Society). Funds multidisciplinary consortia 
 (at least 4 parties\, private partners allowed) to clinically validate kn
 own cancer biomarkers towards use in daily practice\, EUR 0.8-2M per proj
 ect over 2-5 years. An (early) HTA\, biostatistics expertise\, a developm
 ent plan and patient involvement are mandatory. Pre-proposals close 20 Oc
 t 2026 (12:00)\; full proposals 15 Dec 2026-23 Feb 2027\, decision June 2
 027.\n\nhttps://www.kwf.nl/en/forresearchers/funding/validation-of-biomar
 kers-2027
URL:https://www.kwf.nl/en/forresearchers/funding/validation-of-biomarkers-
 2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-257-20261028@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
SUMMARY:Application deadline: COST Open Call OC-2026-1 – New COST Action
 s (research networks)
DESCRIPTION:COST Association. Bottom-up call for new COST Actions\, Europe
 an science and technology networks that fund meetings\, short-term scient
 ific missions\, training schools and dissemination\, not the research its
 elf. A proposal needs at least seven COST member countries\, at least hal
 f of them Inclusiveness Target Countries\, and at least 40% young researc
 hers. Up to 80 Actions may be approved. The collection date is 28 October
  2026\, 12:00 CET.\n\nhttps://www.cost.eu/uploads/2026/03/2026-1-COST_Ope
 n_Call_Announcement.pdf
URL:https://www.cost.eu/uploads/2026/03/2026-1-COST_Open_Call_Announcement
 .pdf
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-151-20261030@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Application deadline: PhRMA Foundation – Value Assessment & Heal
 th Outcomes Research Pre- & Postdoctoral Fellowships 2027
DESCRIPTION:PhRMA Foundation. PhRMA Foundation fellowships in value assess
 ment and health outcomes research: postdoctoral USD 60\,000/yr and predoc
 toral USD 30\,000/yr stipend\, for 12-24 months. The 2027 postdoctoral cy
 cle opened 31 August 2026 and closes 30 October 2026 (noon ET)\; awards a
 nnounced March 2027. The predoctoral page still shows the 2026 cycle (dea
 dline was 30 Oct 2025) and says the 2027 cycle launches soon. Applicants 
 must be at an accredited US university\, so mainly relevant for US-based 
 collaborators.\n\nhttps://www.phrmafoundation.org/grants-fellowships/post
 doctoral-fellowships/value-assessment-health-outcomes-research/
URL:https://www.phrmafoundation.org/grants-fellowships/postdoctoral-fellow
 ships/value-assessment-health-outcomes-research/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-201-20261101@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Sustainability Education Community Fund (UU)
DESCRIPTION:Utrecht University – Pathways to Sustainability. Small grant
 s for bottom-up sustainability-education initiatives at UU such as worksh
 ops\, seminars and pilots\; covers assistance and material costs (incl. t
 ravel and events)\, not teaching-hour reductions. €12\,500 available in
  this round\; decisions 6–8 weeks after the deadline.\n\nhttps://www.uu
 .nl/en/research/sustainability/sustainability-education-and-engagement/fu
 nding
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/research/sustainability/sustainability-education-
 and-engagement/funding
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-5-20261103@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Vidi – Science Domain 2026
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO Vidi for researchers moving into leadership who obtai
 ned their PhD within eight years before 1 October 2026 (extensions possib
 le). Up to EUR 850\,000 for up to five years to build a research line and
  group\; requires an embedding guarantee from a Dutch host institution. S
 cience-domain pre-proposals are due 3 November 2026\, 14:00 CET\; invited
  full proposals are due 6 April 2027\, 14:00 CEST.\n\nhttps://www.nwo.nl/
 en/calls/nwo-talent-programme-vidi-science-2026
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talent-programme-vidi-science-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-10-20261103@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Exploration Call 2027-1
DESCRIPTION:KWF (Dutch Cancer Society). KWF project call for basic and cre
 dentialing research into the biological and psychosocial mechanisms behin
 d cancer onset\, growth\, spread and impact\; relevant for mechanistic wo
 rk on anticancer drugs. Call 2027-1 accepts pre-proposals from 1 Septembe
 r to 3 November 2026 (12:00)\; invited full proposals run 15 February to 
 13 April 2027\, with interviews in June and decisions in August 2027. KWF
  describes this as its last project-based basic-research call before swit
 ching to research group funding from 2028.\n\nhttps://www.kwf.nl/en/forre
 searchers/funding/exploration
URL:https://www.kwf.nl/en/forresearchers/funding/exploration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-98-20261103@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: International Joint Initiative 2026 – Di
 sruptive Technologies for Global Challenges
DESCRIPTION:NWO. International call (NWO with NFRF and other funders) for 
 interdisciplinary consortia of at least three PIs funded by different par
 ticipating agencies\, using disruptive technologies to address the SDGs. 
 NWO funding is limited to projects on SDG 2\, 6\, 7 or 11 and is max EUR 
 760\,000 per project\; the NWO budget was raised to EUR 6.84M in August 2
 026. LOIs were due 9 June 2026\; only invited applicants can now submit f
 ull proposals by 3 November 2026 (NFRF portal)\, with NWO's ISAAC part du
 e 4 November 2026\, 14:00 CET.\n\nhttps://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/2026-intern
 ational-joint-initiative-for-research-harnessing-disruptive-technologies-
 to-address-global-challenges
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/2026-international-joint-initiative-for-re
 search-harnessing-disruptive-technologies-to-address-global-challenges
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-220-20261103@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Vidi – ZonMw Health Research and Medical 
 Sciences Domain 2026
DESCRIPTION:NWO. 2026 Vidi round for the ZonMw Health Research and Medical
  Sciences domain\, aimed at researchers moving into a leadership role who
  obtained their PhD within eight years of 1 October 2026. Up to €850\,0
 00 for a project of up to five years. Two-stage: pre-proposals due 3 Nove
 mber 2026 (14:00 CET)\; invited applicants submit full proposals by 6 Apr
 il 2027 (14:00 CEST). Applications go through Mijn ZonMw and need a dean-
 signed embedding guarantee.\n\nhttps://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talent-pro
 gramme-vidi-health-research-and-medical-sciences-zonmw-2026
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talent-programme-vidi-health-research-
 and-medical-sciences-zonmw-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-7-20261112@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: KIC Demand-driven Research by Consortia 
 – XL
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO KIC call for large public-private consortia tackling 
 societal challenges\, with NWO funding EUR 1.4M-7M per proposal (up to 70
 % of costs) for up to six years and a EUR 14M call ceiling. At least 30% 
 co-funding is required\, part of it private cash. The mandatory pre-propo
 sal deadline was 10 March 2026\; full proposals are due 12 November 2026\
 , 14:00 CET (only for those who submitted a pre-proposal).\n\nhttps://www
 .nwo.nl/en/calls/kic-demand-driven-research-by-consortia-xl
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/kic-demand-driven-research-by-consortia-xl
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-186-20261120@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: SME Call 2027 (MKB Call)
DESCRIPTION:Health~Holland (TKI LSH). Health~Holland call for public-priva
 te R&D projects between SMEs and research organisations (industrial resea
 rch\, TRL 4-6\, max 2 years). Consortia can request EUR 225\,000-450\,000
  in PPP subsidy (research organisations max EUR 150\,000 per project)\, a
 t least EUR 8M total for about 20 projects. The lead applicant must be a 
 Dutch for-profit company\, and all partners must co-finance. Full applica
 tions are due 20 November 2026\, 17:00 CET.\n\nhttps://www.health-holland
 .com/calls/mkb-call-2027
URL:https://www.health-holland.com/calls/mkb-call-2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-176-20261123@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:Expression of interest deadline: CARB-X 2026 Funding Round 2 – A
 ntibacterial Research (all themes)
DESCRIPTION:CARB-X. CARB-X's second 2026 funding round accepts expressions
  of interest from 10 to 23 November 2026 across all four 2026 themes: dir
 ect-acting therapeutics for Gram-negative infections\, the Novel Chemistr
 y for AMR Challenge (target-based therapeutics)\, non-vaccine prevention 
 of neonatal sepsis\, and neonatal sepsis diagnostics. Successful applican
 ts must cover part of the project cost. Funding amounts per award are not
  stated on the application page.\n\nhttps://carb-x.org/apply/application-
 process/
URL:https://carb-x.org/apply/application-process/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-38-20261124@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:Application deadline: MSCA Doctoral Networks 2026
DESCRIPTION:European Commission – MSCA. OPEN. MSCA Doctoral Networks cal
 l HORIZON-MSCA-2026-DN-01 funds international doctoral training networks 
 with 3-year PhD positions and mobility. Opened 28 May 2026\; deadline 24 
 November 2026 (17:00 Brussels). Indicative call budget EUR 593.03M (over 
 130 projects expected). The division already runs the EU2P programme.\n\n
 https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/actions/doctoral-netw
 orks
URL:https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/actions/doctoral-n
 etworks
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-200-20261127@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Utrechts Universiteitsfonds – Funding for 
 researchers (round 6\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Utrechts Universiteitsfonds. Grants for UU employees for resea
 rch visits abroad and for research and education costs (e.g. hiring help\
 , materials\, organising a congress)\, applied for through the UU subsidy
  portal. Six rounds per year\; not every fund type is open in every round
 \, and each fund has its own criteria.\n\nhttps://www.uu.nl/en/organisati
 on/donate/apply-for-subsidies/funding-for-researchers
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/donate/apply-for-subsidies/funding-f
 or-researchers
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-242-20261127@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Utrechts Universiteitsfonds – Student supp
 ort (international exchange/internship)\, round 6 2026
DESCRIPTION:Utrechts Universiteitsfonds. The Utrecht University Fund's stu
 dent programme helps fund an international exchange or internship\, for e
 xample a master's research internship abroad. Applicants must be a Studen
 t Friend of the Fund (€10 a year). Named funds within the Fund may set 
 their own criteria. About €80\,000 a year is available across all stude
 nt grants. In 2026 there are six rounds\, and round 6 runs from 2 to 27 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nhttps://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/donate/apply-for-subsi
 dies/grants-for-students
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/donate/apply-for-subsidies/grants-fo
 r-students
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-247-20261201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Rubicon 2026-3 (postdoc research abroad)
DESCRIPTION:NWO. Lets recent PhD graduates (PhD within 12 months before th
 e deadline\, or a supervisor's declaration that the thesis is approved) s
 pend 12–24 months at a research institute outside the Netherlands. It c
 overs salary\, travel and limited research costs\; the round budget of 
 €3\,145\,000 is shared across the four NWO domains. Applications are in
 dividual and due 1 December 2026\, 14:00.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/en/subs
 idy/rubicon-2026-3
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/en/subsidy/rubicon-2026-3
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-246-20261207@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: GGG – Alledaagse Aandoeningen in de huisa
 rtsenpraktijk (Common Conditions in General Practice)
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. Good Use of Medicines (GGG) round for research on quest
 ions from the NHG general-practice knowledge agenda\, aiming at more effe
 ctive\, safer or more efficient use of medicines already registered in th
 e Netherlands for common conditions. Total budget is €5 million with no
  fixed cap per project\; multicentre studies may be needed. Project ideas
  are due 7 December 2026\; invited full applications are due 31 May 2027\
 , with a decision expected end of October 2027. The applicant must take p
 art in UNH-Research through a university general-practice department.\n\n
 https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/alledaagse-aandoeningen-de-huisartsenpra
 ktijk
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/alledaagse-aandoeningen-de-huisartsen
 praktijk
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-197-20261222@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261223
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: Geneesmiddelen VIMP 2026-1 (Dissemination 
 & Implementation Impulse)
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. VIMP (dissemination and implementation boost) within Zo
 nMw's Goed Gebruik Geneesmiddelen programme\, helping finished ZonMw-fund
 ed research on good medicine use (completed no more than three years ago)
  get used in practice\; dissemination alone is not enough. Max EUR 50\,00
 0 and 18 months per project from a EUR 250\,000 budget\; open since 22 Ju
 ne 2026\, deadline 22 December 2026\, 14:00\, though it may close earlier
  if the budget runs out. Applicant must be a legal entity in the Netherla
 nds\, and applications are in Dutch.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/
 geneesmiddelen-vimp-2026-1
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/geneesmiddelen-vimp-2026-1
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-154-20270101@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Next cut-off deadline: KNMP Stipendiafonds (international study tr
 ip grant)
DESCRIPTION:KNMP. KNMP stipend for pharmacy students at Groningen\, Leiden
  and Utrecht who go abroad for at least two weeks for research that is pa
 rt of their pharmacy study\; applicant must be a candidate KNMP member an
 d must not have started the research yet. Applications are judged three t
 imes a year (closing dates 1 January\, 1 July and 1 October). A 'light' a
 pplication gives EUR 300-500\; a 'heavy' application (meeting at least tw
 o high-potential criteria) can give a higher\, unspecified amount. Each s
 tudent may apply only once.\n\nhttps://www.knmp.nl/beroepsontwikkeling/on
 derzoek/stipendiafonds
URL:https://www.knmp.nl/beroepsontwikkeling/onderzoek/stipendiafonds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-77-20270112@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270113
SUMMARY:Application deadline: ERC Consolidator Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ERC. ERC Consolidator Grant 2027 for researchers 5-15 years af
 ter their PhD (extensions possible for e.g. parental leave). Up to EUR 2M
  for 5 years\, plus up to EUR 1M extra for justified costs. Bottom-up\, a
 ny research topic. The call opened 24 September 2026 and closes 12 Januar
 y 2027.\n\nhttps://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/consolidator-grant
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/consolidator-grant
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-183-20270126@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270127
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: Veni – ZonMw Health Research Domain 2026
 /2027
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO Veni in the ZonMw Health Research and Development dom
 ain: up to EUR 320\,000 for up to three years for researchers with a PhD 
 obtained within three years before 1 January 2026 (or between 1 January a
 nd 2 September 2026). The pre-proposal deadline was 1 September 2026 and 
 no new applications are possible. Applicants with a positive pre-proposal
  decision submit full proposals by 26 January 2027\, 14:00 CET.\n\nhttps:
 //www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talent-programme-veni-health-research-and-devel
 opment-zonmw-2026
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talent-programme-veni-health-research-
 and-development-zonmw-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-46-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-TOOL-01-two-stage – 
 AI for Predictive Biomarkers in Chronic NCDs
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Horizon Europe two-stage RIA HORIZON-HLTH-2027
 -02-TOOL-01-two-stage: developing predictive biomarkers of disease progre
 ssion and treatment response with AI methods for chronic non-communicable
  diseases. EUR 44.2M for about 6 projects of EUR 6-8M. Opens 29 October 2
 026\; first-stage deadline 17 February 2027\, second-stage deadline 16 Se
 ptember 2027. Highly relevant for the division's AI/data science and phar
 macoepi work.\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/
 portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-02-tool-01-tw
 o-stage
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-02-tool-01-two-stage
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-225-20270310@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270310
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270311
SUMMARY:Next cut-off deadline: ERC Proof of Concept 2027 (cut-offs Mar & S
 ep 2027)
DESCRIPTION:ERC. Lump sum of €150\,000 over 18 months for current or rec
 ent ERC grantees who want to test the commercial or societal potential of
  results from their ERC project. Under ERC Work Programme 2027 the call E
 RC-2027-PoC opens 12 November 2026 and has two cut-offs\, 10 March 2027 a
 nd 16 September 2027 (budget €60M\, ~400 grants). The ERC calls these d
 ates provisional.\n\nhttps://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/proof-concept
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/proof-concept
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-156-20270315@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270315
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270316
SUMMARY:Application deadline: PRISMA Proefschrift Prijs 2026 (pharmacy pra
 ctice research)
DESCRIPTION:KNMP. Annual PRISMA Thesis Prize for dissertations defended in
  the previous 2 years at a Dutch or Belgian university\, on new insights 
 from pharmaceutical practice research implemented in community or hospita
 l pharmacy. Evaluated on degree of implementation\, translatability to ph
 armacist care\, and scientific quality. Awarded at the PRISMA symposium (
 12 May 2026\, Breukelen). Submit via prisma@knmp.nl.\n\nhttps://www.knmp.
 nl/beroepsontwikkeling/onderzoek/prisma
URL:https://www.knmp.nl/beroepsontwikkeling/onderzoek/prisma
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-248-20270330@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270330
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270331
SUMMARY:Application deadline: NAM Collaboration Grant 2026 (animal-free me
 thods knowledge transfer)
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. Small grants of up to €30\,000 for up to 12 months to
  transfer animal-free methods (New Approach Methodologies such as organ-o
 n-chip systems and organoids) between a transferring lab and a receiving 
 lab at Dutch research organisations. Each partner must account for at lea
 st 20% of the budget. Applications are assessed in order of arrival until
  30 March 2027\, and the call may close early if the money runs out.\n\nh
 ttps://www.zonmw.nl/en/subsidy/nam-collaboration-grant-2026
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/en/subsidy/nam-collaboration-grant-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-157-20270401@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261009T135014Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270401
